       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of 10 mg. The usual adult range is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily. At 50 mg the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock, and these are hard to reverse because of the drug's long half-life.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily (the standard starting dose)\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily (the maximum dose)\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily (for frail patients or those needing a gentler start)\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, please confirm and tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
